From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben Andersen <sterion@sterion.dk>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:18:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Build on Ubuntu 24.04 with Python 3.11 from deadsnakes

Frigate's wheels are cp311-only and Ubuntu 24.04 ships 3.12, so 3.11 comes
from the deadsnakes PPA. The Debian-only steps (non-free components edit,
trixie backports, deb-src via debian.sources) get their Ubuntu equivalents.
pip runs with --ignore-installed because apt-installed Python modules on the
3.11 path cannot be uninstalled by pip.

PPAs are read from a dated Launchpad snapshot so rebuilds are reproducible.
---
 docker/main/Dockerfile          | 23 ++++++++++++++++-------
 docker/main/build_nginx.sh      |  2 ++
 docker/main/build_sqlite_vec.sh |  2 ++
 docker/main/install_deps.sh     | 32 +++++++++-----------------------
 docker/main/install_ppa.sh      | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 docker/main/install_ppa.sh

diff --git a/docker/main/Dockerfile b/docker/main/Dockerfile
index bf17146..594f426 100644
--- a/docker/main/Dockerfile
+++ b/docker/main/Dockerfile
@@ -6,8 +6,11 @@ ARG DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
 # Globally set pip break-system-packages option to avoid having to specify it every time
 ARG PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES=1
 
-ARG BASE_IMAGE=debian:12
-ARG SLIM_BASE=debian:12-slim
+ARG BASE_IMAGE=ubuntu:24.04
+ARG SLIM_BASE=ubuntu:24.04
+
+# Launchpad PPAs are read as they were at this moment
+ARG PPA_SNAPSHOT=20261020T000000Z
 
 # A hook that allows us to inject commands right after the base images
